{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1225829-creating-a-solo-chronicle-and-needing-some-help","id":1225829,"title":"Creating a solo chronicle and needing some help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-08T00:38:15-07:00","id":1225829,"title":"Creating a solo chronicle and needing some help","content":"Greetings hivemind!<br /> <br /> As I'm stuck in all the strange places with no other player around but my wife I'm preparing our second solo chronicle. I learnt my lesson on Mage: the Awakening game about how to create character for such game (needs to be pro-active not reactive) and about incorporation of backstory and aspirations into the main plot (well, duh!). The cost of that lesson was high (chronicle failed miserably) so I definitely want to make the second shot MUCH better, so that we both don't get discouraged and this is where I need your help. Find logic leaps, plot holes, bring new ideas to the table, and help me make it awesome.<br /> <br /> <b>Assumptions</b>:<br /> We're playing mortal game with supernatural merits. Slightly more of Marvel's Jessica Jones or Daredevil than usual CoD chronicle. I would describe the whole thing as Jessica Jones meets Cthulhu. I'm planning to rely heavily on Second Sight materials but give it slightly 'superpowers' twist to give my player a better chance against what's happening around her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Character</b>:<br /> Ex-police detective, private eye. Yes, inspired by Jessica Jones, but we both came to an agreement that this type of character will be a good fit because it has always tons of reasons to stick her nose into not her businesses. She didn't create a full character yet but as much as I know my wife I'm expecting mix of Social-Physical character, with decent amount of social skills, high investigation and occult. We decided on Psychokinesis (Fire) supernatural merit. She got the 5-dot version, which allows her for both manipulating and creating the fire out of nowhere. I like the merit idea, it will be useful, but I don't think it will be game-breaking (correct me if I don't see anything). The player wants also second 'power' to enhance her strength, I'm still thinking about this.<br /> <br /> The supernatural backstory goes as an accidental fire at house from which she was the only survivor, who 'miraculously' went out unharmed. At least this is what the player remembers. Her parents died in the fire and she was raised by someone else since she was approx. 10. My idea is that the fire was neither accidental, nor her going out was miraculous. It was her first manifestation of the power, which she could hardly control (thus fire at home), but at least she could protect herself (thus unharmed). Digging deeper into the backstory and plot I want the whole story to revolve around the cult of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moloch\" target=\"_blank\">Moloch </a>and she is somehow (spiritually? metaphorically? literally?) related to the god and I want this &quot;fire child&quot; motif to be one of the recurring themes of the campaign.<br /> <br /> Recent story, still not set in stone is that the character was dealing (still as a police detective) with a case during which she got to know about existence of SOME cult and SOME blasphemous rites. Before she managed to crack the case, she was pushed aside by her boss, who took over the case himself and led the raid on cult's HQ or whatever this place was. It ended with a disaster and the lieutenant was the only survivor (guess why). Of course, he put all blame on her and not giving them full information, she had. However, to avoid scandal the whole thing was done quietly, and the player resigned herself from police, leaving some friends and quite few enemies behind her. She\u2019s sure (and rightly so) that the lieutenant was somehow involved in this whole situation and that's why he survived it. <br /> <br /> <b>Setting Basics</b>:<br /> New York, Hell\u2019s Kitchen. MCU reference done on purpose, it will be inspired by what we can see in TV series but of course it\u2019s CoD not superhero game.<br /> <br /> <b>Plot</b>:<br /> For now, I have the first chapter of the chronicle prepared, where player takes a case of a missing boy (see below) and through the course of investigation learns about existence of Moloch cult, confronts with some goons and maybe a single priest. Very little cosmic horror involved so far, and I like it this way. I want the chronicle to slowly unravel in this direction before we go full Cthulhu-style.<br /> <br /> <b>Story synopsis</b>:<br /> Scene 1: Player gets wake-up call on some ungodly hour (4-5am?) from a friend in police that he sent her some people who need her help. Shortly after a gay couple appears and wants to hire her to find their son who got missing. They outline the situation where their apartment got burnt down but their son is missing. Police is not helping at all despite taking the case, so they need help. Hopefully player accepts the case and gets the story going.<br /> Phase 1 Investigation Scenes: I divided investigation into two phases, each phase containing number of clues, any of which can lead further to cracking the case. I want to leave my player maximum freedom on how to tackle the case so I\u2019m not predicting any specific order of clue-finding or importance of them. Should I incorporate the investigation mechanic from CoD corebook into this?<br /> Phase one clues:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>1. Police report on fire causes (obtainable by Contacts; <i>Politics</i> or <i>Computer</i> skills from the Police).</li> <li>2. Police report on the missing boy\u2019s case (obtainable by Contacts or <i>social skills</i> form the Police).</li> <li>3. Zippo found on the fire scene (Obtainable by <i>Investigation</i> skill).</li> <li>4. Description of a possible kidnapper (obtainable by <i>social skills</i> by talking with the neighbours or the doorman in the building).</li> <li>5. Image of the car used by the possible kidnapper and a photoshoot from CCTV camera (obtainable by <i>Computer</i> skill or social skills from the building\u2019s security).</li> <li>6. Information about human-trafficking in New York (obtainable through <i>Streetwise</i> skill)</li> <li>7. Police intel on the case (Obtainable through Contacts by using <i>Socialize</i> skill).</li> </ol>Phase one conclusions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>There is a symbol of a bull\u2019s head in flames (clues 2, 3, 4, 5) that seems important.</li> <li>The appearance of a man who is most likely a kidnaper (clues 4, 5).</li> <li>Police screwed the job terribly, all the conclusions go against the evidence from the crime scene (clues 1, 2, 7).</li> <li>Someone in Police doesn\u2019t want this case to be properly solved (clues 1, 2, 7).</li> </ol>Phase one conclusions are also lead-ins into phase two and each of those four avenues should push the investigation further.<br /> Phase 2 Investigation Scenes: The whole concept of phase two is to bring player to clash with the organisation, although not necessarily naming it, unless the player will make the effort of following actively the lead-in no.1<br /> Phase 2 clues/leads:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>1. The bull\u2019s head symbol is a variation of symbol of an ancient god Moloch who was god of among else fire and demanded human sacrifices (<i>Academics-Research</i>).</li> <li>2. The guy who most likely kidnapped the child is some kind of a strongman or heavy-weight lifter judging simply by his appearance, there are only few places in the city where he could train, visiting the places will eventually result in finding the guy (see below).</li> <li>3. The car was rented by a sports club The Big Bulls and returned 24h ago (<i>Social Skills</i>).</li> <li>4. The Lieutenant (the same who was player\u2019s previous boss) gave direct order marginalise the case and close it ASAP, preferably marking it as an accidental fire that killed the boy. (<i>Social Skills</i>).</li> </ol>The Big Bulls Sports Club Scene: If the player will start looking for the guy she\u2019s eventually end up coming to The Big Bulls Sports Club. She\u2019ll see lots of guys looking similarly to the kidnapper\u2019s photo and clearly knowing something on the topic. If she asks any questions on topic they\u2019ll try to intimidate her and if that doesn\u2019t work \u2013 beat her up (Beaten Down &amp; Surrender Rules?). Squeezing some information from them will require literally beating them to the extent where they are enough afraid to speak.<br /> Confrontation with Lieutenant: Hard to stage but absolutely possible. I don\u2019t know How to stage a proper social manoeuvring situation, so I need some help here. If cleverly approached she may get some information from him (but what? I don\u2019t want to make it to obvious)<br /> Following the Bulls/Lieutenant: If followed each of those can bring the player to the place where the kid is kept (what should it be? I have no good idea for this location). However, the place is heavily guarded so fighting her way through the guards to rescue the kid may be at least difficult (but not impossible, considering the pyrokinetic abilities). The chance to rescue the kid comes after the lieutenant comes in when the whole group starts to prepare for conducting the ritual to praise their god. All of them are there at that time but they are preoccupied which give a player a decent chance of sneaking past them or creating any other plan to actually rescue the kid. If she does nothing the kid will be sacrificed to Moloch by burning alive during the ceremony.<br /> <br /> <b>Comments</b><br /> The story is not long (I assume it should take no more then 8h) nor complex but I think it will be sufficient introduction for the chronicle staging some antagonists and giving a good warm-up. Any comments, ideas how to make it more intriguing, plot holes I didn\u2019t notice, and simply good or bad words are more then welcomed at this stage of my prep.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T04:48:27-07:00","id":1225841,"title":"","content":"Some questions:<br /> <br /> \u25cb What is the range of antagonists and the degree of their capability? Mostly vanilla mortal? Average mortal, some exceptional?<br /> \u25cb What kind of followup links do you want to have? Is someone higher up in the police department giving the Lieutenant the okay? Are there other cults in the area operating? Other supernatural groups that might show interest?<br /> \u25cb What &quot;settings&quot; are you planning to include? Any of the major gamelines or their attendant metaphysics (like Spirits and the Shadow, the God-Machine and Angels, etc.)?<br /> \u25cb What kind of consequences can you see assuming various conclusions?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I'd use the Investigation system for this. It seems ideal for this scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T05:15:18-07:00","id":1225847,"title":"","content":"Vent0, thanks for joining in! Answerimg your questions:<br /> <br /> - antagonists: vanilla mortals both average ad exceptional, cultists, spirits (aka demons), horrors. Some supernal powers involved.<br /> - I don't plan introducing any major splats permanently, mayne as guest starring. If anything then spirits and shadow and god machine. Still unsure if anything at all<br /> - My idea was to make lieutenant one of the major antagonists for now so he will play a major role in the Bull's Cult. Perhaps the cult could back him up and support his Police career which is accelerating now. This thought seems tempting, now that you asked about it. Other supernatural groups? I don't know yet. But this is the area where I definitely welcome suggestions<br /> - For now I see 2 possible conclusions (boy lives or dies) and I'm still thinking about follow-up. Do I kess something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T18:16:55-07:00","id":1226000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1225829-creating-a-solo-chronicle-and-needing-some-help?p=1225847#post1225847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- antagonists: vanilla mortals both average ad exceptional, cultists, spirits (aka demons), horrors. Some supernal powers involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Spirits are in play, Abjuration and Exorcism are available. If your PC needs help, maybe an opposing (beneficent or not) cult can assist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1225829-creating-a-solo-chronicle-and-needing-some-help?p=1225847#post1225847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- I don't plan introducing any major splats permanently, mayne as guest starring. If anything then spirits and shadow and god machine. Still unsure if anything at all</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering for metaphysics reasons. Knowing what splats are in play clarifies options regarding forces and factions that might be interested. For instance, if Vampires are around, they might be interested in a fire cult causing problems and take steps to curb them. Same with Werewolves and Spirits getting uppity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1225829-creating-a-solo-chronicle-and-needing-some-help?p=1225847#post1225847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- My idea was to make lieutenant one of the major antagonists for now so he will play a major role in the Bull's Cult. Perhaps the cult could back him up and support his Police career which is accelerating now. This thought seems tempting, now that you asked about it. Other supernatural groups? I don't know yet. But this is the area where I definitely welcome suggestions</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a mysterious higher up means there is still another threat to investigate <i>and</i> the character cannot trust the police still after the lieutenant is removed. Webs within webs lets you stretch out suspense and drama (and Chronicle life).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1225829-creating-a-solo-chronicle-and-needing-some-help?p=1225847#post1225847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- For now I see 2 possible conclusions (boy lives or dies) and I'm still thinking about follow-up. Do I kess something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what if the kid survives unharmed by the fire? The PC has Pyrokinesis, right? What if she hides in view of the ceremony and uses it to prevent the fire from harming the kid. Pretty sure the cult is going to be thrown when that happens. Her busting up the cult herself, vs with outside help, vs with Internal Affairs help will all have different long term outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T18:25:14-07:00","id":1226002,"title":"","content":"Possible monkey wrench that could be sent your way.<br /> <br /> Bull and male physical fitness, screams <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithraism\" target=\"_blank\">Mithras</a> more than Moloch. Be ready just in case.<br /> <br /> and the PC might also try to see if there has been other mysterious death of children in burning houses that were quickly shut down. She might suspect an Arsonist or a Pyromanic. Be ready for that line of investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T23:27:29-07:00","id":1226026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1225829-creating-a-solo-chronicle-and-needing-some-help?p=1226002#post1226002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible monkey wrench that could be sent your way.<br /> <br /> Bull and male physical fitness, screams <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithraism\" target=\"_blank\">Mithras</a> more than Moloch. Be ready just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take a look into that, thanks. Moloch is depicted with bull's head thus the idea and I really liked the human sacrafices idea but \u00cc'll definitely take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T07:36:31-07:00","id":1226071,"title":"","content":"That is true. And it's not like either religion/faith has the monopoly on Bull symbolic, there is also Knossos in Crete with the Minotaur and bull jumping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T17:43:49-07:00","id":1226148,"title":"","content":"Something I cooked up, inspired by the plot and synopsis:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Burned Horn (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Burned Horn is a modern-day cult dedicated to the worship of Moloch, known in contemporary times as a Canaan god of fire and sacrifice, though interpretations vary. Its worshippers are said to have practiced child sacrifice, and the Burned Horn is one of many who continue it to this day. In return they are given authority among lesser men and power in times of need.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Purpose</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: (insert the cult's existing purpose here)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Relic</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: (insert the cult's focal point of faith here)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Doctrine</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: (insert the cult's rules and traditions here)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Cultists</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: (insert stereotypical cultists here)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Initiation Benefits</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Initiates are taught basic mythology and symbology dedicated to Moloch and its peers. They gain a Canaanite Faiths specialty in either Academics or Occult.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Even the least initiates find themselves invigorated by their god once they claim full membership. They gain the Hardy Merit at one dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> The Burned Horn is younger than it claims to be, but it is old enough to have entrenched itself in the community. The cultists gains two dots to divide among the Allies, Contacts, or Status Merits.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> The priests of Moloch are graced with their god's power. They gain the Psychokinesis (Fire) Merit at three dots.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> The high priests of Moloch are no mere worshippers, for they are the very furnaces that feed the god. They gain the Sacrificial Offering Merit (as per</span></span> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Hurt Locker</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">) at three dots. The high priests do not suffer breaking points when using the Merit, and once per chapter may &quot;reset&quot; its incremental number of successes required by burning bits of themselves together with the sacrifice. The burnt flesh must constitute at least a level of lethal damage.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}